<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Depreciation: value of an asset after T years (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A {@asset@} is bought for Ksh \( {@P0@} \). Every year it depreciates by \( {@R0@}\% \) of its value at the beginning of that year.</p>
<p>Give your answers to the nearest shilling.</p>
<p>(a) Find its value after 1 year.</p>
<div>Value after 1 year \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Find its value after \( {@T0@} \) years.</p>
<div>Value after \( {@T0@} \) years \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) How much value has it lost altogether in the \( {@T0@} \) years?</p>
<div>Loss in value \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> \( {@P0@} - \frac{ {@R0@} }{100} \times {@P0@} = {@P0@}\left(1 - \frac{ {@R0@} }{100}\right) = {@V1@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Each year the value at the start of the year is multiplied by \( 1 - \frac{ {@R0@} }{100} = {@float(1 - R0/100)@} \), so</p>
\[ A = P\left(1 - \frac{R}{100}\right)^T = {@P0@} \times ({@float(1 - R0/100)@})^{ {@T0@} } = {@round(A0)@}. \]
<p><strong>(c)</strong> Loss \( = {@P0@} - {@round(A0)@} = {@P0 - round(A0)@} \).</p>
<p>Depreciation is calculated on the <em>current</em> value, so the amount lost each year gets smaller: in year 1 it loses \( {@P0 - V1@} \), but in year 2 only \( {@round(V1 - V1*(1 - R0/100))@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
